{"type":"step-attempt","step":"design","sessionId":"8868ca72-0328-4c2b-b986-3b96428a21bf","outcome":{"verdict":"success","findingsPath":null,"error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"reason":"Wrote design.md, spec.md, tasks.md under specrunner/changes/cancel-process-tree-kill/. Design captures the 5 architect-approved decisions (jobId-gated shared pid resolver, process-death-gate replacing status gate, leader-gated group SIGKILL via kill(-pid,0) probe, runner-owned QueryAbortHub abort seam reusing the per-call AbortController, output changes), with rationale + rejected alternatives, risks, and open questions. Spec has 5 SHALL/MUST requirements with Given/When/Then scenarios mapping every acceptance criterion. Tasks T-01..T-09 are granular with file paths and per-task acceptance criteria; existing pinned cancel suites kept green (isGroupLeader optional-with-default, 'no PID recorded' substring preserved, running-path SIGTERM preserved). Scope-outs respected; adapter→core/port boundary respected; ADR path left to adr-gen.","status":"success"},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-11T05:50:35.888Z","endedAt":"2026-08-11T06:07:01.684Z","commitOid":"752c3326a17be7d39978ff901cfd3be56f243dbd"}
